From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kim Hansen <github@kimhansen.dk>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:34:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Tests: no reply a server can send traps the client

ResponseFuzzTests builds a well-formed reply for every response parser
(SMB2 commands, NTLM challenge, DCERPC/NetShareEnum, file and
file-system information classes, Direct TCP framing), then decodes every
truncation of it and 2,000 seeded corruptions per parser; each must
decode or throw ResponseDecodingError. MalformedServerTests runs the
same guarantee end to end against a scripted localhost server: short,
oversized and truncated frames, zero negotiated sizes, a compound reply
missing a part, a NextCommand inside the header, an over-long READ, a
READ that never advances, and 300 corrupted compound replies over the
wire. Neither suite needs the Samba container.

RUMSKROT-TESTS

